== Strengthening the assumptions

Consider
$
  L=sum_(j=0)^m a_j D^j, quad m in NN.
$

Assume that $f,a_0,dots,a_m$ are *real analytic* on an open interval $I$,
and $a_m$ is not identically zero.

We allow $a_m$ to have zeros. Pointwise convergence will still imply
an analytic limit satisfying $L g=g$.
